      "text": "1. **Prime Factorization**:\n   - First, we need to determine the prime factorizations of 18 and 42.\n   - The prime factorization of 18 is:\n     \\[\n     18 = 2 \\times 3^2\n     \\]\n   - The prime factorization of 42 is:\n     \\[\n     42 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7\n     \\]\n\n2. **Greatest Common Divisor (GCD)**:\n   - The GCD is found by taking the lowest power of all common prime factors.\n   - The common prime factors of 18 and 42 are 2 and 3.\n   - The lowest power of 2 in both factorizations is \\(2^1\\).\n   - The lowest power of 3 in both factorizations is \\(3^1\\).\n   - Therefore, the GCD is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{GCD} = 2^1 \\times 3^1 = 2 \\times 3 = 6\n     \\]\n\n3. **Least Common Multiple (LCM)**:\n   - The LCM is found by taking the highest power of all prime factors present.\n   - The prime factors are 2, 3, and 7.\n   - The highest power of 2 in the factorizations is \\(2^1\\).\n   - The highest power of 3 in the factorizations is \\(3^2\\).\n   - The highest power of 7 in the factorizations is \\(7^1\\).\n   - Therefore, the LCM is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{LCM} = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 = 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 = 126\n     \\]\n\n4. **Product of GCD and LCM**:\n   - Now, we calculate the product of the GCD and the LCM:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Product} = \\text{GCD} \\times \\text{LCM} = 6 \\times 126\n     \\]\n   - Performing the multiplication:\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 126 = 756\n     \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of 18 and 42 is \\(\\boxed{756}\\).",
