      "text": "1. **Prime Factorization:**\n   - Begin by finding the prime factorizations of both numbers:\n     \\[\n     18 = 2^1 \\cdot 3^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     42 = 2^1 \\cdot 3^1 \\cdot 7^1\n     \\]\n2. **Greatest Common Divisor (GCD):**\n   - The GCD is found by taking the lowest power of each prime factor present in both factorizations:\n     - The common prime factors are \\(2^1\\) and \\(3^1\\).\n     - Therefore, the GCD is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{GCD} = 2^1 \\cdot 3^1 = 2 \\cdot 3 = 6\n     \\]\n\n3. **Least Common Multiple (LCM):**\n   - The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime factor present in either factorization:\n     - The prime factors are \\(2^1\\), \\(3^2\\), and \\(7^1\\).\n     - Therefore, the LCM is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{LCM} = 2^1 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 7^1 = 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 7 = 126\n     \\]\n\n4. **Product of GCD and LCM:**\n   - Now, we need to find the product of the GCD and the LCM:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Product} = \\text{GCD} \\times \\text{LCM} = 6 \\times 126\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculation of the Product:**\n   - Perform the multiplication:\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 126 = 756\n     \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{756}\n\\]",
